    "problem": "The factors causing abrupt transitions between strong and weak Atlantic circulation regimes during glacial periods remain unclear, as evidence challenges the traditional view that massive iceberg discharges are the sole trigger, suggesting additional control factors are needed to explain these climate shifts.",
    "method": "This paper proposes a mechanism, simulated using a coupled climate model, in which gradual atmospheric CO2 changes trigger abrupt shifts in Atlantic ocean circulation by altering atmospheric moisture transport across Central America and modulating the North Atlantic freshwater budget.",
    "task": "The task is to use a coupled atmosphere-ocean model to investigate whether gradual changes in atmospheric CO\u2082 can trigger abrupt shifts in the Atlantic meridional overturning circulation, explaining millennial-scale climate variability in a glacial climate state.",
